4. All subjects must provide tumor tissue samples for PD-L1 testing: Tumor tissue samples should preferably be newly obtained tumor tissues. For subjects who cannot provide newly obtained tissues, tumor tissue samples archived within 3 years prior to the first study treatment can be provided. The sample type should be neutral formalin-fixed and paraffin-embedded \[FFPE\] tissue wax blocks or at least 6 unstained tumor tissue sections. If the number is less than 6 pieces, it is necessary to negotiate with the sponsor and only allow enrollment after obtaining consent.
5. ECOG overall performance status (PS) 0-1 point;
